      "id": "phrase-un-par-de",
      "kind": "phrase",
      "promptEs": "un par de cosas",
      "questionEn": "How do you say “a couple of” before a plural noun?",
      "answerEn": "Use un par de, then the plural noun.",
      "noteEn": "The literal idea is a pair, but conversational un par de often gives an approximate small quantity. The noun after de is plural: un par de días, un par de preguntas.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Tengo un par de preguntas.",
        "en": "I have a couple of questions."
      },
      "tags": [
