    {
      "id": "word-nos--pronominal-marker",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "nos",
      "answerEn": "no separate English word here; marks a “we” verb that is used with nos",
      "noteEn": "Some Spanish verbs conventionally come with me, te, se, nos, or os even when no one literally acts on themselves. Nos marks the form for a group that includes the speaker. English usually absorbs it into the verb's meaning.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Nos quejamos del ruido.",
        "en": "We complain about the noise."
      },
      "tags": [
        "word",
